WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:04.570
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:05.970
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.530
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.790
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.950
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你们带来了终极《办公室》粉丝播客。

6
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:17.430
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

7
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.610
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
分享幕后细节，还有许多我们闺蜜之间的故事。

8
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.670
We're the Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

9
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.810
Hi there.
大家好。

10
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:27.370
Hello.
你好。

11
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:33.530
Hey, so today on Office Ladies, we have a very special interview with the person I call
嘿，今天在《办公室女士》节目中，我们请到了一位非常特别的嘉宾，我称他为

12
00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.470
the architect of The Office.
《办公室》的建筑师。

13
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.810
It is our editor and director, Dave Rogers.
他就是我们的剪辑师兼导演，戴夫·罗杰斯。

14
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.090
I like how you just jumped right in with it today, Ange.
安吉，我喜欢你今天这么直接切入主题的样子。

15
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.770
What is happening in the new year?
新的一年发生了什么？

16
00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.290
Are you becoming me?
你是在变得像我吗？

17
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.310
I think so.
我想是的。

18
00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.610
Because look, I'm taking us on a tangent.
因为你看，我正要把我们带离正题。

19
00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.870
Should I read my diary, my journal?
我是不是该读读我的日记了？

20
00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.250
And I'm just like, let's get to it.
而我却只想说，咱们直接开始吧。

21
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.370
I feel like I want to.
我觉得我想读。

22
00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.310
I want to.
我想读。

23
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.930
What's happened this year?
今年发生了什么？

24
00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:56.590
I don't know.
我不知道。

25
00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.630
I feel like my 2025 mantra is, let's get to it.
我觉得我2025年的座右铭就是：直接开始吧。

26
00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:00.330
Okay.
好吧。

27
00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.210
Well, let's get to it then.
那我们就直接开始吧。

28
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:08.110
And Dave Rogers worked on The Office from 2005 to 2013.
戴夫·罗杰斯从2005年到2013年一直参与《办公室》的制作。

29
00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.830
He started as our editor.
他最初担任我们的剪辑师。

30
00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:14.090
But then, as you all know, he started directing in season five.
但正如你们所知，他在第五季开始担任导演。

31
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:20.550
In total, Dave edited 95 of the original broadcast episodes, and he directed eight of them.
戴夫总共剪辑了95集原始播出的剧集，并执导了其中8集。

32
00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.530
He knows the show better than anyone.
他比任何人都了解这部剧。

33
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:27.450
Well, Angela, I guess you are going to share some digital clutter with us now.
好吧，安吉拉，我想你现在要和我们分享一些数字杂物了。

34
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.570
So you are staying in your wheelhouse in a way.
所以你某种程度上还是在你的舒适区里。

35
00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:32.170
I'm a combo.
我是个混合体。

36
00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.910
Oh, it's combo gear.
哦，是混合装备。

37
00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:34.850
It's combo gear.
是混合装备。

38
00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.590
It's, yeah, I'm a combo platter.
是啊，我是个混合拼盘。

39
00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.810
2025 is let's get to it, but also let's share it a little bit.
2025年的主题是“直接开始”，但也稍微分享一下。

40
00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.790
I'm really liking this.
我真的很喜欢这样。

41
00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:47.330
So I did share with Jenna that I found something pretty fun in my digital clutter,
我确实和珍娜分享过，我在我的数字杂物里发现了一些挺有趣的东西，

42
00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.570
and I'm excited to share it with you all.
我很兴奋能和大家分享。

43
00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.050
So I have talked about this before on the podcaSt.
我在播客里以前提到过这个。

44
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.830
Years ago, when the show was on the air, I teamed up with the NBC Digital folks,
多年前，当剧集还在播出时，我和NBC数字部门的人合作过，

45
00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:00.110
with Joya and Scott and Carol, all those folks.
和乔亚、斯科特、卡罗尔，还有所有那些人一起。

46
00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:00.710
They're awesome.
他们太棒了。

47
00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:04.770
And we did a little series for the website called Adventures with Angela.
我们为网站制作了一个小系列，叫《安吉拉的冒险》。

48
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:05.990
They were so cute.
它们太可爱了。

49
00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.150
They are all these videos of you kind of showing different aspects of the show.
那全是你展示剧集不同侧面的视频。

50
00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.510
You would introduce different actors or different crew members.
你会介绍不同的演员或不同的剧组成员。

51
00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.930
And you sent me this one, Angela.
还有你发给我的这一条，安吉拉。

52
00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.970
It's cute patoot galore.
简直可爱到爆。

53
00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.630
I had so much fun doing these.
做这些视频我玩得太开心了。

54
00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:23.790
They're just little behind the scenes of life on the set of The Office.
它们只是《办公室》片场生活的一些幕后花絮。

55
00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:29.410
Well, the one I sent Jenna was the week I went into Dave's editing bay.
嗯，我发给珍娜的那条是我去戴夫剪辑室的那周拍的。

56
00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.050
We found the footage.
我们找到了那段素材。

57
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.790
I thought it would be so fun to hear it.
我觉得把它放出来听听会很有趣。

58
00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.650
I'm going to share it in stories as well.
我也会把它分享到快拍里。

59
00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.270
And it just took us right back.
那段记忆瞬间把我们拉回了过去。

60
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.270
Hello, NBC.com.
你好，NBC.com。

61
00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.310
We have a behind the scenes exclusive with Dave Rogers,
我们有戴夫·罗杰斯的独家幕后采访，

62
00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.170
one of our fabulous editors on the show.
他是我们剧组出色的剪辑师之一。

63
00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:45.510
That's Dave.
那就是戴夫。

64
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.530
It's also donut cart day.
今天还是甜甜圈餐车日。

65
00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.050
Oh, mini donuts.
噢，迷你甜甜圈。

66
00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.170
It's ridiculous.
太离谱了。

67
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:52.270
Did you get any?
你拿到了吗？

68
00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:52.970
I did not.
我没拿到。

69
00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:53.710
Not yet.
还没呢。

70
00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:54.070
Yeah.
是啊。

71
00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:54.950
They're so good.
它们太好吃了。

72
00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.090
I'll take one.
我要拿一个。

73
00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.290
Dave Rogers worked on The Single Guy.
戴夫·罗杰斯曾参与过《单身汉》的制作。

74
00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.030
Seinfeld.
《宋飞正传》。

75
00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:00.610
Wow.
哇。

76
00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:01.710
News Radio.
《新闻广播台》。

77
00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:02.410
Entourage.
《明星伙伴》。

78
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.970
Do you have any entourage stories?
你有关于《明星伙伴》的八卦吗？

79
00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:08.190
Come on.
快说嘛。

80
00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:09.370
Those guys, they're wild.
那些家伙，他们太狂野了。

81
00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:10.090
They're crazy, right?
他们很疯狂，对吧？

82
00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:14.810
I was in an edit bay far away from all the locations that they shoot on that show.
我的剪辑室离他们拍摄的那些外景地很远。

83
00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.150
He's online.
他在线了。

84
00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.070
Editors know everything.
剪辑师什么都知道。

85
00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:16.790
I'm absolutely sure.
我绝对肯定。

86
00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:17.930
You hear everything.
你们什么都能听到。

87
00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:19.830
They hear everyone's conversations.
他们能听到所有人的谈话。

88
00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:20.170
Okay.
好吧。

89
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.590
You've been with The Office since the pilot.
你从试播集开始就一直跟着《办公室》了。

90
00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.490
I came on right after the pilot.
我是试播集之后立刻加入的。

91
00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:25.830
I tweaked a little bit in the pilot.
我在试播集里稍微做了一些调整。

92
00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.270
This isn't right.
这不对。

93
00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.170
You gave me the wrong thing.
你给错我东西了。

94
00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.490
Before we broadcaSt.
在播出之前。

95
00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.670
Dave was a first-time director this season, you guys.
戴夫这一季第一次当导演，大家伙儿。

96
00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.530
It was really awesome.
真的很棒。

97
00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:33.310
Thank you.
谢谢。

98
00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.390
You know the show so well.
你对这部剧太了解了。

99
00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:38.190
I have to say, I'm pretty, like, blown away by, I mean, because he sort of sits here and
我不得不说，我真的，挺震惊的，我是说，因为他平时就坐在这儿，

100
00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.430
watches take after take after take.
一遍又一遍地看着拍摄素材。

101
00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:39.750
I do.
我愿意。

102
00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:45.110
One thing I'm learning right here and now is that the editor's room, a little toasty.
我现在学到的一件事就是，剪辑室里有点闷热。

103
00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:45.610
Yeah.
是啊。

104
00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:46.610
A little toasty.
有点闷热。

105
00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.310
Can we talk about your desk for a second?
我们能聊聊你的办公桌吗？

106
00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:49.590
Yeah.
好啊。

107
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:50.950
Yeah, let's talk about my desk.
好，聊聊我的桌子吧。

108
00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:51.630
Who's this guy?
这家伙是谁？

109
00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:52.570
That's Bryce.
那是布莱斯。

110
00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:53.490
Bryce!
布莱斯！

111
00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:53.970
Yeah.
没错。

112
00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.150
You're so cute.
你太可爱了。

113
00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.250
Sometimes he comes in.
他偶尔会过来。

114
00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:00.670
I almost brought him in today because I knew you were coming in, and as a tribute to you
我今天本来想带他来的，因为我知道你要来，而且为了向你致敬，

115
00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.410
in the Super Bowl episode, having your little cat, Bandit, in the drawer.
在超级碗那一集里，你把你的小猫班迪特放在了抽屉里。

116
00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.470
You were going to have Bryce in the drawer.
你本来打算把布莱斯放进抽屉里。

117
00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.130
Well, Bryce, here, if you can swing this way.
嗯，布莱斯，来，如果你能转到这边的话。

118
00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.670
This is where Bryce, he does hang out in the closet.
这就是布莱斯待的地方，他确实会待在壁橱里。

119
00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:14.170
He's got a little bed, and I've got stuff, food, and toys.
他有个小床，我还有些东西、食物和玩具。

120
00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.630
I wonder if you were the inspiration for that high-tech stuff here.
我在想，你是不是这些高科技装备的灵感来源。

121
00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:22.140
I want to touch all the knobs so bad.
我好想摸摸这些旋钮。

122
00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:24.380
Yes.
是的。

123
00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.300
No product placement, but what are we talking about here?
虽然不是植入广告，但我们在这儿说的是什么？

124
00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.200
Do we have dry skin?
我们皮肤干燥吗？

125
00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:29.960
Yes.
是的。

126
00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.700
You can feel how warm and dry this room is.
你能感觉到这个房间有多暖和、多干燥。

127
00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:33.240
It is very warm in here.
这里确实很暖和。

128
00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.560
So I try to keep moisture up.
所以我尽量保持水分。

129
00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:35.900
You try to keep moisture up.
你尽量保持水分。

130
00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.180
Yes.
是的。

131
00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.400
I never used to, but then the ladies are always like, your hand feels like an alligator.
我以前从不这样，但后来女士们总说，你的手摸起来像鳄鱼皮一样。

132
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.920
Too much information.
信息量太大了。

133
00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.900
I don't want to know what the ladies say.
我不想知道女士们说了什么。

134
00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.520
What does this mean right here?
这儿这个是什么意思？

135
00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:46.720
What's this?
这是什么？

136
00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.520
Those are technical things.
那是些技术设备。

137
00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.240
Can I tell you?
我能告诉你吗？

138
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.280
This looks like something that would be in Lost, and that they would show for a whole season
这看起来像是《迷失》里会出现的东西，他们会展示一整季，

139
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.300
and then say it means nothing.
然后说它毫无意义。

140
00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:58.820
That picture of Dean, that's our other editor, Dean Holland.
那张迪恩的照片，那是我们的另一位剪辑师，迪恩·霍兰德。

141
00:04:59.200 --> 00:04:59.560
Yes.
是的。

142
00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.260
And Dave, and they won an Emmy for our show, which was amazing.
还有戴夫，他们为我们的剧集赢得了艾美奖，这太棒了。

143
00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.700
It was the episode, The Job.
那是《工作》那一集。

144
00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.380
Jenna and I presented at the Eddie Awards when you guys won.
你们获奖时，我和珍娜在艾迪奖上颁奖。

145
00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.200
For the Academy of Cinema Editors.
为美国电影剪辑师协会颁奖。

146
00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:10.640
Yes.
是的。

147
00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:17.320
And we got a big laugh because Jenna talked about an editor's room being dark and sweaty.
我们当时引起了一阵大笑，因为珍娜说剪辑室又黑又闷。

148
00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:17.580
Yeah.
没错。

149
00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.120
And I said that it's the place where this noise comes from.
我说那是发出这种噪音的地方。

150
00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.630
Here, I'll show you what that sounds like.
来，我让你听听那是什么声音。

151
00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:31.150
For a cat.
给猫用的。

152
00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:32.390
Awesome.
太棒了。

153
00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.730
I should be on Saturday Night Live.
我应该去上《周六夜现场》。

154
00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.230
I can do my rewind, girl.
我可以做我的倒带，姑娘。

155
00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.130
Angela, we can't write a skit for that.
安吉拉，我们不能为此写个短剧。

156
00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:44.430
Really?
真的吗？

157
00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.310
Because it's gold.
因为这可是金点子。

158
00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:50.110
Angela, these are amazing.
安吉拉，这些太棒了。

159
00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.250
You are an amazing interviewer.
你是一位出色的采访者。

160
00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:59.070
You discussed mini donuts, moisturizing his hands, the knobs in the room.
你聊了迷你甜甜圈、他手部的保湿，还有房间里的旋钮。

161
00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:02.990
I just went through his office and pointed out everything on his desk.
我只是翻了他的办公室，指出了他桌上的每一样东西。

162
00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:03.630
Poor Dave.
可怜的戴夫。

163
00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:04.650
He's such a good sport.
他真是个好脾气的人。

164
00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:08.290
He did show me the closet where his dog Bryce would hang out.
他确实带我看了他那只叫布莱斯的狗待的壁橱。

165
00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.190
I loved Bryce.
我喜欢布莱斯。

166
00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.930
Bryce had a bed, a blanket, a toy.
