456
00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:02.840
And I wondered how you did it, Dave.
我当时还在想你是怎么做到的，戴夫。

457
00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:04.940
But now that I know about the dupe detector.
但现在我知道了重复检测器的存在。

458
00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:10.460
So Michael has a talking head about how charming he is.
迈克尔有个采访片段，讲他自己有多迷人。

459
00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:10.760
Yes.
是的。

460
00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.800
But then he's yelling at Ryan, what'd you do to my desktop?
但转头他又在冲瑞安大喊，你对我的桌面做了什么？

461
00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:14.860
Where's my maps?
我的地图去哪了？

462
00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:15.900
Where are my maps?
我的地图在哪？

463
00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.560
But then he goes back to the talking head, but it's overlaid over each other.
然后他又切回采访片段，但画面是重叠在一起的。

464
00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.940
And I was like, how did they do that?
我当时就在想，他们是怎么做到的？

465
00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:22.800
But this is how.
原来是这样。

466
00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.680
Well, this is what some of that.
嗯，这就是其中一部分原因。

467
00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:27.380
I mean, the dupe detector just helps us to see, hey, is there stuff that we're
我的意思是，重复检测器只是帮我们看看，嘿，有没有什么素材是

468
00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:29.820
that was, you know, from the assembly that was cut out?
你知道的，是从初剪版里删掉的？

469
00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:31.340
That's the first thing that we do.
这是我们做的第一件事。

470
00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:34.260
But stuff like that, then it's editing again.
但像那样的东西，就属于二次剪辑了。

471
00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.900
It's like, oh, we have other footage.
就像是，哦，我们还有其他素材。

472
00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:39.120
That stuff may have been in the assembly, like him yelling at Ryan.
那些素材可能在初剪版里，比如他冲瑞安大喊的那段。

473
00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:39.800
It may not be.
也可能不在。

474
00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:41.040
That just might be in dailies.
那可能只是在每日样片里。

475
00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:42.100
I mean, it's a.
我的意思是，这是一个。

476
00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.900
You have so many things to look through.
你有太多的东西需要去翻看。

477
00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:45.160
But we'll go through the assembly.
但我们会过一遍初剪版。

478
00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:47.180
And then I'll see also if scenes.
然后我也会看看有没有其他场景。

479
00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:48.160
I mean, that's the thing even.
我的意思是，即使是那样。

480
00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:52.560
I like to say if there's a scene that's in the assembly, a lot of times a scene that
我喜欢说，如果有一个场景在初剪版里，很多时候一个

481
00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:56.360
was deleted is the same as the deleted scene on the DVDs.
被删掉的场景和DVD里的删减片段是一样的。

482
00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:58.560
But that means it wasn't really polished.
但这说明它并没有真正经过精修。

483
00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.420
Like it was taken out in the assembly stage.
就像它是在初剪阶段被拿掉的。

484
00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.820
Like we lost it when we were doing the director's cut.
就像我们在做导演剪辑版时把它弄丢了一样。

485
00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:08.260
So we've thrown it on the DVD and maybe we've polished it a little bit for the, you know,
所以我们把它扔到了DVD里，也许我们为了DVD的发行，

486
00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:09.380
to go to the DVDs.
稍微精修了一下。

487
00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:13.520
But now I have the freedom to kind of go in and clean stuff up.
但现在我有自由去深入清理一些东西。

488
00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:18.000
We'll add music if we need to, like where we didn't have the budget for it on the DVDs.
如果需要的话，我们会加上音乐，比如那些在DVD时期我们没预算加音乐的地方。

489
00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:20.340
I mean, sometimes I've watched some of the deleted scenes.
我的意思是，有时候我看了一些删减片段。

490
00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:23.000
I'm like, I can hear the director, you know, things like that.
我会觉得，我能听到导演的声音，你知道，诸如此类。

491
00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:25.640
Like so things can get cleaned up, you know, which is nice.
所以有些东西可以被清理得更好，你知道，这挺好的。

492
00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.800
I have a couple of rules.
我有几条原则。

493
00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:29.400
Oh, let's hear them.
哦，说来听听。

494
00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:32.760
So I never change a take of the show.
我从不更改剧中的拍摄镜头。

495
00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:38.260
Like I feel that this is the documentary crew have come in and they've gotten more time
我觉得这就像是纪录片摄制组进驻了，他们有了更多的时间

496
00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:39.860
to make these episodes longer.
来把这些剧集做得更长。

497
00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:43.380
So they're just adding in more stuff that they've shot.
所以他们只是在增加更多他们拍摄的素材。

498
00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.620
So I'll never change a performance or very, very rarely.
所以我从不更改表演，或者说极少更改。

499
00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:49.460
There might be something where I'm like, oh, I need, you know,
可能会有那么一些情况，我会觉得，哦，我需要，你知道，

500
00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:54.080
I'll change a camera angle occasionally, but I'll never, you won't see a different take.
我偶尔会改变一下摄像机角度，但你绝不会看到不同的表演镜头。

501
00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:57.520
If Michael says something this way, I'm not going to, you know,
如果迈克尔是这样说的，我就不会，你知道的，

502
00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:59.800
go to a different take of him saying the same line.
去用他讲同一句台词的其他拍摄版本。

503
00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.080
I will only add, you know, and this is for all of you.
我只想补充一点，你知道的，这是对你们所有人说的。

504
00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:06.320
I don't want any kind of parallel universes or anything out there.
我不希望出现任何平行宇宙之类的东西。

505
00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:08.060
So I appreciate that.
所以我很感激这一点。

506
00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:09.920
That's like the integrity of the show.
这关乎节目的完整性。

507
00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:13.640
So as you're making these super fan episodes,
所以当你们制作这些超级粉丝剧集时，

508
00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:16.940
you are doing it as if you are the documentary filmmaker.
你们要以纪录片制作人的身份来做。

509
00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:17.420
Yeah.
是的。

510
00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:23.360
And what has already aired is like, yeah, is sacred.
而已经播出的内容，就像，是的，是神圣不可侵犯的。

511
00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:23.940
Yes.
没错。

512
00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:28.020
I mean, every once in a while, like a reaction shot might come out
我的意思是，偶尔会有一些反应镜头出现，

513
00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:31.200
because we've added more dialogue or something like that.
因为我们增加了更多的对话之类的东西。

514
00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:33.520
And that was used to cover a gap, let's say.
那通常是为了填补空白，比方说。

515
00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:36.120
But generally like no performance changes.
但总的来说，表演内容没有改变。

516
00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:39.440
The other thing is that there's no alternate things.
另一件事是，没有其他的替代版本。

517
00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:42.060
Like for example, season three, the job finale.
比如，第三季，《工作》那一集结尾。

518
00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:47.540
We have footage of Karen sitting on at a fountain outside the building crying
我们有凯伦坐在大楼外喷泉边哭的镜头，

519
00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:51.540
and she gets a phone call and she accepts the job.
她接了个电话，然后接受了那份工作。

520
00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:56.500
So this was like, we shot that because we didn't, we, I guess we weren't sure which way we were going to go.
所以，我们拍了那个，因为我们当时，我想我们不确定最终会选哪种走向。

521
00:22:56.900 --> 00:22:57.960
Yeah, you didn't get the job.
是啊，你没得到那份工作。

522
00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:02.610
You know, so we shot, you know, that's not going back into a show because it doesn't, you know,
你知道，所以我们拍了那个，但那不会放回剧集里，因为它，你知道，

523
00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:04.470
it doesn't track with everything we've seen.
它与我们所看到的一切不符。

524
00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:09.610
But I do see, you know, there are things like that that pop up and I'm like, no, we can't use that.
但我确实看到，你知道，会有那种东西冒出来，我就想，不行，我们不能用那个。

525
00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:10.790
That's a different path.
那是另一条路了。

526
00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:16.710
You know, we really do our best not to contradict things and, you know, not to have continuity errors, things like that.
你知道，我们真的尽力不去自相矛盾，你知道，不去制造连续性错误之类的东西。

527
00:23:16.790 --> 00:23:16.910
Right.
对。

528
00:23:17.050 --> 00:23:20.070
Keep the purity of the story arc as it was intended.
保持故事线如初衷般纯粹。

529
00:23:20.070 --> 00:23:25.210
I remember doing every once in a while those alternate versions of scenes.
我记得偶尔会拍那些场景的替代版本。

530
00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:34.470
And I think there's an alternate version of Jim and Pam walking out of the elevator at the end of the job or something.
我想在《工作》那一集结尾，吉姆和帕姆走出电梯时，有一个替代版本之类的。

531
00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:36.850
Or Jim walking out or me walking out.
或者吉姆走出来，或者我走出来。

532
00:23:36.990 --> 00:23:40.250
I remember we were trying to figure out that moment.
我记得我们当时在琢磨那个时刻。

533
00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:40.650
Right.
对。

534
00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:41.230
We did that.
我们确实拍了。

535
00:23:41.290 --> 00:23:44.090
We did shoot that alternate version of you guys in the elevator.
我们确实拍了你们在电梯里的那个替代版本。

536
00:23:44.710 --> 00:23:46.670
I don't know if you're in it and he comes in.
我不确定你是否在里面，然后他进来了。

537
00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:48.010
That's what I couldn't remember either.
那也是我记不清的地方。

538
00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:49.650
I feel like I sent it to you at the time.
我觉得我当时发给你过。

539
00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:50.550
I think you did.
我想你确实发过。

540
00:23:50.790 --> 00:23:52.890
You were like, do you remember how we did these alternates?
你当时说，你还记得我们是怎么拍这些替代版本的吗？

541
00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:53.250
Yeah.
是的。

542
00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:55.390
You were probably doing your super fan episode.
你当时可能正在做你的超级粉丝剧集。

543
00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:58.690
But that was the best, you know, I mean, what we got with the job.
但那是最好的，你知道，我的意思是，我们在《工作》那一集里呈现的效果。

544
00:23:58.810 --> 00:24:01.530
That moment is just great when he comes in, when you're like, yeah.
他走进来的时候那个瞬间太棒了，当你表现出，嗯，是的。

545
00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:03.670
And then it's like, hey, are you free for dinner?
然后就像是，嘿，你今晚有空吃晚饭吗？

546
00:24:03.870 --> 00:24:04.790
And you're like, yeah.
然后你说，有空。

547
00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:05.390
Yeah.
是的。

548
00:24:05.430 --> 00:24:07.070
Your look is so, so beautiful.
你的表情真是，太美了。

549
00:24:07.410 --> 00:24:07.830
What was I saying?
我刚才说到哪了？

550
00:24:07.990 --> 00:24:10.910
You know, and it's just, there's so many little gems like that.
你知道，像这样的小亮点真的太多了。

551
00:24:11.070 --> 00:24:14.330
Although I did find the rehearsal for the proposal.
虽然我确实找到了求婚的那场排练。

552
00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:15.230
Oh.
哦。

553
00:24:15.330 --> 00:24:18.750
And, you know, that we shot on the back lot very far away.
而且，你知道，我们在很远的后场拍的。

554
00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:23.490
But we have, you know, on our back lot by the trailers, the post trailer in the back,
但我们有，你知道，在我们的后场，拖车旁边，后面的后期制作拖车里，

555
00:24:23.610 --> 00:24:25.370
I guess Paul Feig, it's weight loss.
我猜是保罗·费格，那是《减肥》那一集。

556
00:24:25.550 --> 00:24:27.330
It was Paul Feig who directed weight loss.
是保罗·费格执导的《减肥》那一集。

557
00:24:27.550 --> 00:24:30.190
And it was his idea to do this big rehearsal?
那是他提议进行这次大型排练的吗？

558
00:24:30.590 --> 00:24:30.810
Yeah.
是的。

559
00:24:31.090 --> 00:24:34.670
But we shot like, you know, Jim proposing to Pam.
但我们拍了，你知道，吉姆向帕姆求婚的场景。

560
00:24:34.670 --> 00:24:37.350
We wanted to see how it would look just being so far away.
我们想看看从那么远的地方拍出来是什么效果。

561
00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:39.550
I remember that now that you say it.
你这么一说我倒想起来了。

562
00:24:39.590 --> 00:24:39.750
Yeah.
是啊。

563
00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:42.350
It was so trippy.
那感觉太奇幻了。

564
00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:48.150
And I remember now that I was a little bit like, can't you do this with stand-ins?
我现在记得当时我心里有点犯嘀咕，难道不能用替身来拍吗？

565
00:24:48.210 --> 00:24:55.130
Because when Jim goes down on one knee for Pam, like that's such a big moment for our characters.
因为当吉姆为帕姆单膝下跪时，那对我们的角色来说是一个非常重要的时刻。

566
00:24:55.190 --> 00:25:00.810
And I don't want to like do it here in the parking lot as a screen test or a camera teSt.
我不想把它当作试镜或摄像测试，就在停车场里演一遍。

567
00:25:00.810 --> 00:25:02.570
You want to live it the first time.
你想在正式拍摄时去体验它。

568
00:25:02.570 --> 00:25:02.890
I want to save it.
我想把它留到那一刻。

569
00:25:02.890 --> 00:25:03.150
Yeah.
没错。

570
00:25:03.350 --> 00:25:06.630
And I want there to be cars whizzing by and I want there to be rain.
我希望当时有车呼啸而过，我希望当时下着雨。

571
00:25:06.930 --> 00:25:07.570
We got all that.
我们确实都拍到了。

572
00:25:07.590 --> 00:25:09.590
But somehow you guys convinced me.
但不知怎么的，你们说服了我。

573
00:25:09.590 --> 00:25:12.190
And I do remember going out in the parking lot that day.
我确实记得那天去了停车场。

574
00:25:12.290 --> 00:25:15.930
Well, I didn't even know this existed though until I found it.
嗯，我甚至不知道它的存在，直到我发现了它。

575
00:25:15.930 --> 00:25:18.070
Well, I guess those guys convinced me.
好吧，我想是那些家伙说服了我。

576
00:25:18.070 --> 00:25:19.550
Yeah, I never – because Dean –
是啊，我从来没——因为迪恩——

577
00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:20.690
I didn't know that.
我不知道那件事。

578
00:25:21.130 --> 00:25:26.730
There are things like that that I've never seen before, you know, because I didn't edit all the episodes.
有些东西我以前从未见过，你知道，因为我并没有剪辑所有的剧集。

579
00:25:26.750 --> 00:25:36.090
So when I'm working on an episode that I didn't originally cut, there are things that I find where I'm like, oh my gosh, like this is amazing.
所以当我处理一集我最初没有剪辑过的剧集时，我会发现一些让我觉得“天哪，这太棒了”的东西。

580
00:25:36.090 --> 00:25:48.230
I can't imagine how much amazing sort of like reliving a chapter of our lives that you get to do because I know just for us when I find a deleted scene or a blooper I haven't seen,
我无法想象你重温我们生活中的一个篇章是多么美妙，因为我知道，仅仅对我们来说，当我发现一个我没看过的删减片段或花絮时，

581
00:25:48.450 --> 00:25:53.410
it just warms my heart and just immediately makes me happy just remembering that time.
它总是让我心里暖暖的，一想到那段时光，我就立刻感到快乐。

582
00:25:53.570 --> 00:25:58.610
Is that part of this job for you, Dave, is you open up all these old folders of our lives?
戴夫，这对你来说是这份工作的一部分吗？打开我们生活中所有这些旧文件夹？

583
00:25:58.790 --> 00:26:00.350
Like do you have moments of nostalgia?
比如，你会感到怀旧吗？

584
00:26:00.670 --> 00:26:01.350
Oh, always.
哦，总是会。

585
00:26:01.570 --> 00:26:01.790
Yeah.
是啊。

586
00:26:01.790 --> 00:26:05.110
But I've just been so involved with the show for so long.
但我参与这部剧太久了。

587
00:26:05.230 --> 00:26:14.370
It's not like it really went away and especially since people, you know, are always – I guess my algorithm, my social media, everything, you know.
它并没有真正离我远去，尤其是因为人们，你知道，总是——我想我的算法，我的社交媒体，所有的一切，你知道。

588
00:26:14.550 --> 00:26:15.030
The office.
《办公室》。

589
00:26:15.410 --> 00:26:15.470
Yeah.
没错。

590
00:26:15.830 --> 00:26:20.470
But like even just, you know, my nephews, like they reached a certain age, then they became huge fans.
但即使是，你知道，我的侄子们，当他们到了某个年龄，就成了这部剧的忠实粉丝。

591
00:26:20.470 --> 00:26:20.730
Yeah.
是啊。

592
00:26:20.730 --> 00:26:25.770
And I'm constantly, you know, just meeting people who are – you know, they just love the show and they're discovering it.
我经常，你知道，遇到一些人，他们——你知道，他们就是很喜欢这部剧，而且正在发掘它。

593
00:26:25.870 --> 00:26:27.090
And it's easy to see why.
这很容易理解为什么。

594
00:26:27.090 --> 00:26:28.790
It's really funny and enjoyable.
它真的很有趣，很耐看。

595
00:26:28.790 --> 00:26:34.570
And just there's so many things that happen throughout the course of the series, you know.
而且在整个系列中发生了太多事情，你知道。

596
00:26:34.730 --> 00:26:38.490
So, I mean, like I could pontificate about that for, you know, hours.
所以，我的意思是，我可以就此高谈阔论，你知道，几个小时。

597
00:26:38.610 --> 00:26:44.570
But it's, you know, I'll sit there and stop and watch and laugh and, you know, I still enjoy it, you know.
