不过那真的很疯狂。

1245
00:53:34.110 --> 00:53:35.450
Just pulling up.
刚开车过去。

1246
00:53:35.630 --> 00:53:37.850
And then the first person we see is Sergio.
然后我们见到的第一个人就是塞尔吉奥。

1247
00:53:38.190 --> 00:53:39.850
And then we walk a few steps.
接着我们走了几步。

1248
00:53:40.170 --> 00:53:40.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1249
00:53:40.610 --> 00:53:41.790
Then we walk a few steps.
然后我们又走了几步。

1250
00:53:41.830 --> 00:53:42.870
And then there's Kasha.
接着就看到了卡莎。

1251
00:53:43.110 --> 00:53:45.330
Then we see Kelly Cantley in the hallway.
然后我们看到凯莉·坎特利在走廊里。

1252
00:53:45.330 --> 00:53:46.890
And then there you are.
然后你就出现在那里了。

1253
00:53:47.050 --> 00:53:47.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1254
00:53:47.330 --> 00:53:48.450
I mean, it just was.
我是说，当时就是那样。

1255
00:53:48.670 --> 00:53:50.070
It was so special.
真的很特别。

1256
00:53:50.410 --> 00:53:50.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1257
00:53:50.910 --> 00:53:51.170
Yeah.
没错。

1258
00:53:51.330 --> 00:53:51.710
It was.
确实如此。

1259
00:53:52.110 --> 00:53:54.970
It is really nice to see familiar faces.
看到熟悉的面孔真是太好了。

1260
00:53:55.210 --> 00:53:55.730
I mean, Veda.
我是说，维达。

1261
00:53:56.070 --> 00:53:56.430
Yes.
是的。

1262
00:53:56.430 --> 00:53:57.530
So Arne is there.
阿恩也在那儿。

1263
00:53:58.070 --> 00:53:58.550
Rusty.
拉斯蒂。

1264
00:53:58.550 --> 00:53:59.810
Rusty Mahmood.
拉斯蒂·马哈茂德。

1265
00:53:59.910 --> 00:54:00.590
Mahmood is there.
马哈茂德也在那儿。

1266
00:54:01.210 --> 00:54:03.810
So there are a lot of, you know, familiar faces.
所以有很多，你知道，熟悉的面孔。

1267
00:54:04.390 --> 00:54:06.070
And that's, you know, it's always nice.
这，你知道，总是很棒。

1268
00:54:06.250 --> 00:54:08.590
We had such a great, great group of people on the show.
我们在剧组里有一群非常非常棒的人。

1269
00:54:08.670 --> 00:54:08.950
We really did.
我们确实有。

1270
00:54:08.950 --> 00:54:09.490
Such a great crew.
非常棒的团队。

1271
00:54:09.670 --> 00:54:10.310
So it's nice.
所以感觉很好。

1272
00:54:10.470 --> 00:54:13.830
And there's a lot of great new people that I've been working with, too.
而且我也一直在和很多很棒的新人合作。

1273
00:54:14.070 --> 00:54:14.450
So it's, you know.
所以，你知道。

1274
00:54:14.450 --> 00:54:16.790
That you will tell us about at some point.
你以后会告诉我们的。

1275
00:54:17.050 --> 00:54:17.470
That's right.
没错。

1276
00:54:17.610 --> 00:54:23.050
So we can bug them when the paper comes out for all the details on how they designed that set and did those props.
这样等文章发表时，我们就能去烦他们，问问他们是怎么设计那个布景和制作那些道具的所有细节了。

1277
00:54:23.770 --> 00:54:24.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1278
00:54:24.210 --> 00:54:28.470
I will say it was really nice seeing you guys come in on the set.
我得说，看到你们走进片场真的很好。

1279
00:54:28.550 --> 00:54:30.330
And just like, oh.
就像是，噢。

1280
00:54:30.430 --> 00:54:30.910
And everybody.
还有大家。

1281
00:54:31.150 --> 00:54:33.410
I mean, you guys got a huge round of applause and everything.
我是说，你们受到了热烈的掌声之类的。

1282
00:54:33.650 --> 00:54:43.070
Everybody was just very, you know, just they know what you guys have done and what you guys have brought to, you know, television and this universe, this office universe.
每个人都非常，你知道，他们都知道你们所做的一切，以及你们为，你知道，电视和这个宇宙，这个办公室宇宙所带来的贡献。

1283
00:54:43.070 --> 00:54:45.650
And, you know, it means a lot.
而且，你知道，这意义重大。

1284
00:54:45.710 --> 00:54:46.810
You guys are royalty.
你们是皇室成员。

1285
00:54:47.170 --> 00:54:47.530
Aw.
噢。

1286
00:54:47.530 --> 00:54:47.850
Really.
真的。

1287
00:54:48.210 --> 00:54:48.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1288
00:54:48.770 --> 00:54:49.410
That's so nice.
太好了。

1289
00:54:49.430 --> 00:54:50.030
You know.
你知道。

1290
00:54:50.350 --> 00:54:51.450
I was afraid.
我当时很担心。

1291
00:54:51.670 --> 00:54:53.370
Honestly, I knew you guys were coming.
老实说，我知道你们要来。

1292
00:54:53.470 --> 00:54:55.830
I was like, oh, the cast is going to be intimidated.
我当时想，噢，演员们会感到紧张的。

1293
00:54:56.070 --> 00:55:00.810
Like, are they going to be, you know, I hope they're not, like, all super nervous, you know.
就像，他们会，你知道，我希望他们不会，你知道，超级紧张。

1294
00:55:01.130 --> 00:55:01.450
Aw.
噢。

1295
00:55:01.450 --> 00:55:03.050
But they're pros, everybody.
但他们都是专业人士，每个人。

1296
00:55:03.430 --> 00:55:04.110
They're lovely.
他们都很可爱。

1297
00:55:04.590 --> 00:55:11.990
I feel like I can reveal this one thing because I found it really charming, which is that we also got to tour the writer's space.
我觉得我可以透露这一件事，因为我觉得它真的很迷人，那就是我们还参观了编剧的工作区。

1298
00:55:12.130 --> 00:55:12.450
Yes.
是的。

1299
00:55:12.450 --> 00:55:20.690
Which was really neat when I went into the writer's room and they had all the cards on the board, just like we had cards on the board.
当我走进编剧室时，看到板子上贴满了卡片，就像我们以前在板子上贴卡片一样，这真的很棒。

1300
00:55:20.870 --> 00:55:31.990
But then I looked over at the episode that you were shooting and there were three photographs from the office and they were shots of us in cars driving.
但后来我看向你们正在拍摄的那一集，上面有三张来自《办公室》的照片，那是我们开车时的镜头。

1301
00:55:32.830 --> 00:55:45.990
And I asked about it and Kelly said, oh, yeah, that's because we have some driving shots coming up and we were just looking at for research, how do you shoot in a car?
我问起这件事，凯莉说，哦，对，那是因为我们接下来要拍一些车内镜头，我们当时正在做研究，看看怎么拍车内戏？

1302
00:55:46.270 --> 00:55:46.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1303
00:55:46.630 --> 00:55:49.510
And Greg was saying the lipstick cameras and you.
格雷格提到了微型摄像机，还有你。

1304
00:55:49.670 --> 00:55:51.190
I'm the one who provided the pictures.
照片是我提供的。

1305
00:55:51.530 --> 00:55:52.950
Oh, of course.
哦，当然。

1306
00:55:53.230 --> 00:55:54.070
And I was, yeah.
我当时就说，对。

1307
00:55:54.310 --> 00:55:55.890
I took a picture of them.
我拍了那些照片。

1308
00:55:56.070 --> 00:55:56.690
I did too.
我也拍了。

1309
00:55:57.070 --> 00:55:57.970
I was there.
我就在现场。

1310
00:55:58.370 --> 00:55:59.430
I was in one of them.
其中一张里还有我。

1311
00:55:59.630 --> 00:55:59.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1312
00:56:00.190 --> 00:56:01.650
Well, yeah, because we should.
嗯，对，因为我们确实应该那样做。

1313
00:56:01.810 --> 00:56:04.850
I think yours was probably Andy's Ancestry.
我想你那张应该是《安迪的祖先》那一集。

1314
00:56:05.130 --> 00:56:05.370
Yes.
没错。

1315
00:56:05.370 --> 00:56:06.690
It was me and Nellie.
是我和内莉。

1316
00:56:06.750 --> 00:56:07.290
You and Nellie.
你和内莉。

1317
00:56:07.410 --> 00:56:08.350
And I had directed that one.
那一集是我执导的。

1318
00:56:08.450 --> 00:56:09.250
So I had that one.
所以我才有那张照片。

1319
00:56:09.370 --> 00:56:11.590
And there was one of Michael and Daryl.
还有一张是迈克尔和达里尔的。

1320
00:56:12.010 --> 00:56:12.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1321
00:56:12.350 --> 00:56:13.230
And that was another one I did.
那也是我执导的另一集。

1322
00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:14.590
That was an employee transfer.
那是《员工调动》那一集。

1323
00:56:15.510 --> 00:56:20.270
Those were ones I directed because I had, I remember just struggling, like, how are we going to do the camera angles?
那些都是我执导的，我记得当时很纠结，心想我们要怎么处理摄像机角度呢？

1324
00:56:20.370 --> 00:56:21.930
Like, what do we, you know, because you have to choose.
就是，我们该怎么做，你知道的，因为你必须做出选择。

1325
00:56:22.150 --> 00:56:27.430
You don't, you know, when you're shooting an interior car scene and you have the, what we call the lipstick caMs.
当你拍摄车内场景时，你不需要，你知道的，我们有所谓的微型摄像机。

1326
00:56:27.570 --> 00:56:27.690
Right.
没错。

1327
00:56:27.770 --> 00:56:29.490
You can only get so many cameras in there.
你没法在车里放太多摄像机。

1328
00:56:29.490 --> 00:56:29.950
Yep, right.
对，没错。

1329
00:56:30.070 --> 00:56:32.150
So it's like, do you want the, you know, a raking shot?
所以就在想，你是想要一个斜拍镜头吗？

1330
00:56:32.290 --> 00:56:33.070
Do you want a single?
还是想要一个单人镜头？

1331
00:56:33.270 --> 00:56:38.930
What, you know, so this, we were just looking at these kinds of frames and to say, like, hey, this is, you know, what we're going for.
什么，你知道的，所以我们当时只是在看这些画面，想说，嘿，这就是我们要的效果。

1332
00:56:39.070 --> 00:56:44.490
And I had a conversation with the DP afterwards because she wanted to show, like, the camera.
后来我和摄影指导聊过，因为她想把摄像机拍进去。

1333
00:56:44.630 --> 00:56:47.570
She's like, well, we should see the cameras, you know, when we're outside the car.
她说，嗯，我们在车外的时候应该能看到摄像机才对。

1334
00:56:47.670 --> 00:56:48.090
I'm like, nope.
我说，不行。

1335
00:56:48.570 --> 00:56:53.030
I'm like, whenever we did this on the show, we would not, that's the precedent.
我说，我们在拍这部剧时从来不那样，这是惯例。

1336
00:56:53.030 --> 00:56:59.870
Whatever we, you know, we would have these lipstick cams, but sometimes we would have, you know, we would go film the actual car and you wouldn't see them.
无论我们，你知道的，我们会有这些微型摄像机，但有时我们会去拍真实的汽车，你不会看到它们。

1337
00:56:59.950 --> 00:57:01.370
We didn't want to obscure the actors' faces.
我们不想遮挡演员的脸。

1338
00:57:01.430 --> 00:57:05.510
We just buy that these are very, very tiny cameras that are in there.
我们只要默认这些是非常非常小的摄像机放在里面就行了。

1339
00:57:05.510 --> 00:57:06.750
That's such a good point.
说得太好了。

1340
00:57:07.010 --> 00:57:16.230
So this is so interesting then because you are now on the paper preserving the look of the office because it's the documentary crew.
这太有意思了，因为你现在在纸面上保留了《办公室》的视觉风格，因为它就是纪录片摄制组拍的。

1341
00:57:16.410 --> 00:57:17.630
It's the same documentary crew.
是同一个纪录片摄制组。

1342
00:57:17.650 --> 00:57:19.790
So they will have shot it the same way.
所以他们会用同样的方式拍摄。

1343
00:57:19.990 --> 00:57:22.510
There's still some new things that they can do.
他们当然还是可以做一些新的尝试。

1344
00:57:22.530 --> 00:57:27.810
But, yes, there are certain things that, you know, like this is the point is that it exists in this universe.
但是，是的，有些事情，你知道的，重点就是它存在于这个宇宙中。

1345
00:57:27.970 --> 00:57:31.390
We're not doing like a – I mean there are so many mockumentary shows out there right now.
我们不是在做那种——我的意思是现在市面上有很多伪纪录片剧集。

1346
00:57:31.390 --> 00:57:38.910
And, you know, that's one thing I'll say, Greg, you know, he kind of wanted to get back to basics with, you know, the style of the office.
而且，你知道的，我要说的一点是，格雷格，他想回归本源，回归《办公室》的风格。

1347
00:57:38.950 --> 00:57:43.010
And like I don't want to have – feel like there's 15 cameras around, you know.
我不想让人感觉周围有15台摄像机，你知道的。

1348
00:57:43.170 --> 00:57:43.390
Yeah, right.
是啊，没错。

1349
00:57:44.030 --> 00:57:55.630
And so, you know, and there have been a lot of, I think, important creative decisions on just, you know, everything from the casting to the set to the, you know,
所以，你知道的，我认为在很多重要的创意决策上，从选角到布景，再到，你知道的，

1350
00:57:55.770 --> 00:57:57.850
style of the show and what we're doing.
剧集的风格以及我们正在做的事情。

1351
00:57:58.430 --> 00:57:59.190
So, yeah.
是啊，没错。

1352
00:57:59.250 --> 00:58:00.330
Well, we're excited.
嗯，我们很兴奋。

1353
00:58:00.410 --> 00:58:01.530
We're excited to see it.
我们很期待看到它。

1354
00:58:01.650 --> 00:58:01.700
Yeah.
没错。

1355
00:58:02.070 --> 00:58:04.390
Last question for you, Dave, before you leave.
戴夫，在你离开之前，问你最后一个问题。

1356
00:58:04.770 --> 00:58:09.890
You had mentioned that you still have a bottle of champagne in your fridge from Aaron Sorkin.
你提到过你的冰箱里还有一瓶亚伦·索尔金送的香槟。

1357
00:58:10.090 --> 00:58:10.550
Yes.
是的。

1358
00:58:10.670 --> 00:58:12.050
Will you tell that story?
能讲讲那个故事吗？

1359
00:58:13.090 --> 00:58:14.010
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1360
00:58:14.350 --> 00:58:18.010
Well, one day we got – Greg shared an email with us.
有一天我们收到——格雷格和我们分享了一封邮件。

1361
00:58:18.170 --> 00:58:22.730
I guess Aaron Sorkin had written – Aaron Sorkin, you know, the great writer who's done –
我想是亚伦·索尔金写的——亚伦·索尔金，你知道的，那位伟大的编剧，他创作过——

1362
00:58:22.730 --> 00:58:27.130
I mean, just A Few Good Men, The West Wing, one of my favorite shows.
我是说，光是《好人寥寥》、《白宫风云》就是我最喜欢的剧集之一。

1363
00:58:27.250 --> 00:58:29.050
He did The Newsroom, another amazing show.
他还创作了《新闻编辑室》，那是另一部了不起的剧。

1364
00:58:29.370 --> 00:58:35.890
He had written Greg a letter and he just said how much he loved the office, the writing, the cast, the editing.
他给格雷格写了一封信，信里说他有多喜欢《办公室》，喜欢里面的剧本、演员阵容和剪辑。

1365
00:58:36.230 --> 00:58:36.910
Do you remember –
你还记得吗——

1366
00:58:36.910 --> 00:58:39.110
Greg printed it out and put it up at craft services.
格雷格把它打印出来贴在了茶水间。

1367
00:58:39.430 --> 00:58:39.480
Yeah.
没错。

1368
00:58:39.490 --> 00:58:48.590
That wall that we had to walk past to get on the soundstage had, you know, people's wedding announcements, a baby photo of whoever had just had a baby.
那面我们去摄影棚必经的墙上，贴着大家的结婚请柬，还有刚生了宝宝的人晒出的婴儿照。

1369
00:58:48.590 --> 00:58:52.090
And then this letter from Aaron Sorkin in the middle.
然后中间就贴着这封亚伦·索尔金的信。

1370
00:58:52.330 --> 00:58:52.490
Yeah.
没错。

1371
00:58:53.110 --> 00:58:57.490
And he had given Greg like a case of Don Perignon.
他还送了格雷格一箱唐·培里侬香槟。

1372
00:58:58.070 --> 00:59:00.710
So I got a bottle and it's still in my fridge.
所以我拿了一瓶，它现在还在我冰箱里。

1373
00:59:01.010 --> 00:59:02.850
How many years have you had that?
你留了多少年了？

1374
00:59:03.330 --> 00:59:04.490
I mean, how many years?
我是说，到底多少年了？

1375
00:59:04.930 --> 00:59:05.570
15 years?
15年？

1376
00:59:05.710 --> 00:59:06.370
When did we get it?
我们是什么时候收到的？

1377
00:59:06.550 --> 00:59:07.590
When did it get – I don't know.
什么时候收到的——我不知道。

1378
00:59:08.070 --> 00:59:08.990
A long time ago.
很久以前了。

1379
00:59:09.010 --> 00:59:09.910
When are you going to open it?
你打算什么时候开它？

1380
00:59:09.910 --> 00:59:10.430
I don't know.
我不知道。

1381
00:59:12.150 --> 00:59:14.650
There are times where I wanted to and then other people are like, oh, no, no, no.
有时候我想开了它，但其他人会说，噢，不，不，不。

1382
00:59:14.650 --> 00:59:15.550
You want to save that.
你要留着它。

1383
00:59:15.910 --> 00:59:16.630
It's so good.
那可是好东西。

1384
00:59:16.630 --> 00:59:19.830
Like, you don't want to just drink it on New Year's or do – you know, and I'm like, all right.
就是说，你不想只是在新年或者什么日子随随便便喝掉它，你知道的，所以我就想，好吧。

1385
00:59:19.930 --> 00:59:22.210
It's just a living in the fridge.
它就一直待在冰箱里。

1386
00:59:22.450 --> 00:59:25.670
Maybe this year or next year I'll make sure I drink it.
也许今年或者明年我一定要把它喝了。

1387
00:59:26.390 --> 00:59:27.530
Does anybody want to share?
有人想一起分享吗？

1388
00:59:27.870 --> 00:59:28.830
Yeah, come over.
好啊，过来吧。

1389
00:59:29.230 --> 00:59:31.290
We'll come over for some Aaron Sorkin champagne.
我们会过去喝亚伦·索尔金的香槟。

1390
00:59:31.410 --> 00:59:33.470
Let's have some – we'll watch a super fan episode.
我们喝点酒，再看一集超级粉丝版剧集。

1391
00:59:33.570 --> 00:59:33.970
How's that?
怎么样？

1392
00:59:34.150 --> 00:59:34.730
Oh, yes.
噢，太好了。

1393
00:59:34.830 --> 00:59:35.470
I love that.
我喜欢这个主意。

1394
00:59:35.730 --> 00:59:36.330
I love that.
我喜欢这个主意。

1395
00:59:36.410 --> 00:59:36.830
All right.
好吧。

1396
00:59:36.870 --> 00:59:38.410
Well, Dave, we love you so much.
戴夫，我们非常爱你。

1397
00:59:38.550 --> 00:59:39.810
Thank you for being here today.
谢谢你今天能来。

1398
00:59:39.830 --> 00:59:40.310
Love you, Dave.
爱你，戴夫。

1399
00:59:40.390 --> 00:59:40.750
Thank you.
谢谢。

1400
00:59:40.850 --> 00:59:41.510
Thanks for having me.
谢谢你们邀请我。

1401
00:59:41.590 --> 00:59:43.890
It's really – I love your show.
真的——我太喜欢你们的节目了。

1402
00:59:43.890 --> 00:59:47.030
So we're going to talk more about the Star Wars holiday special.
所以我们接下来要多聊聊《星球大战》假日特辑。

1403
00:59:51.270 --> 00:59:52.690
But I love you guys.
但我真的很喜欢你们。

1404
00:59:52.770 --> 00:59:53.530
I love what you're doing.
我喜欢你们正在做的事情。

1405
00:59:53.850 --> 00:59:55.550
And yeah, I'm a fan.
没错，我是你们的粉丝。

1406
00:59:55.670 --> 00:59:56.030
I'm a fan.
我是粉丝。

1407
00:59:56.350 --> 00:59:57.430
Aw, thanks, Dave.
噢，谢谢你，戴夫。

1408
00:59:57.710 --> 00:59:58.330
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1409
01:00:02.540 --> 01:00:04.700
Dave Rogers is the beSt.
戴夫·罗杰斯是最棒的。

1410
01:00:05.000 --> 01:00:05.580
The beSt.
最棒的。

1411
01:00:05.900 --> 01:00:08.820
Dave, thank you so much for being in studio with us today.
戴夫，非常感谢你今天来到我们的演播室。

1412
01:00:08.820 --> 01:00:09.700
We just love you.
我们真的很喜欢你。

1413
01:00:09.700 --> 01:00:14.100
And we want to say thank you to Dave and his whole team for treating our show with such
我们要感谢戴夫和他的整个团队，感谢他们如此

1414
01:00:14.100 --> 01:00:14.940
love and care.
用心且充满爱意地对待我们的节目。

1415
01:00:15.120 --> 01:00:18.040
You can check out all of the super fan episodes on Peacock.
大家可以在 Peacock 上观看所有的超级粉丝剧集。

1416
01:00:18.120 --> 01:00:20.760
And we can't wait to get Dave's must-watch liSt.
我们已经迫不及待想看到戴夫的必看清单了。

1417
01:00:20.980 --> 01:00:21.440
I know.
我知道。

1418
01:00:21.900 --> 01:00:22.660
Thanks, everyone.
谢谢大家。

1419
01:00:22.800 --> 01:00:23.620
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1420
01:00:23.740 --> 01:00:24.380
Have a great one.
祝大家过得愉快。

1421
01:00:24.480 --> 01:00:25.100
Have a good one.
祝大家过得愉快。

1422
01:00:25.640 --> 01:00:35.180
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

